  "limitations": [
    "This approval is scoped to P07 Winsqlite3 persistence, migrations, integrity recovery, backup, authority, and concurrency plus retained G04-G06 regressions. Runtime MCP, UI, packaging, installation, upgrade, profiling, and endurance remain assigned to later phases and gates.",
    "The tests exercise deterministic process, cancellation, deadline, namespace-race, sidecar-injection, hard-link, sharing, and sparse-size failures; they do not emulate machine power loss or storage-controller cache loss.",
    "ADR P07-003 retains the same-token instruction-level check/use residual boundary for P22 hardening. P07 tests cover pre-existing and deterministically injected role, hard-link, and replacement attacks, not arbitrary hostile same-token code after the final boundary.",
    "A dedicated allocator-fault seam after final backup publication is not present. The independent review verified the publication rollback owner structurally, while runtime tests cover collision, cancellation, stale-stage, sidecar, race, and hard-link boundaries.",
    "Late sidecar substitution at migration receipt validation is established by retained exact-role/identity control flow and adjacent runtime injection tests; there is no separate runtime seam at that exact instruction boundary.",
    "Frozen retained-handle VFS behavior is exercised transitively by SQLite verification; explicit EOF-straddling xRead and concurrent disjoint-offset callback unit tests remain recommended follow-up coverage.",
    "The exact successful 4-GiB leaf and 8-GiB cohort boundaries are not physically materialized at runtime. Cap-plus-one sparse rejection and overflow-safe source inspection prove fail-closed enforcement above each boundary.",
    "SQLite shared-memory sidecar bytes are intentionally not treated as stable evidence because the file is a volatile WAL index; the no-checkpoint regression instead uses exact Main/WAL bytes, nonzero WAL, stable identities, and reopen visibility."
  ],
